<title>POLAND: Vistula mulls laying off 206 employees.</title>
<headline>Vistula mulls laying off 206 employees.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish garment maker Vistula SA is considering laying off 206 of the 500 workers at one of its plants as it shifts production from exports, the daily Parkiet quoted the director of the plant in Przeworsk, southern Poland, as saying.</p>
<p>&quot;About 60 percent of the plant's production is geared toward export, which has become unprofitable....If I accepted cheap orders I would lead the plant to ruin,&quot; Stanislaw Inglot told Parkiet in its Saturday edition.</p>
<p>On Friday, garment maker Bytom said in a statement it would lay off 288 workers in February to cut production and shut down one of its six plants.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
